*> Implementation test of client/src/dimfx.cob (docs/protocol/39-portals.md section 9, 37-nether-3 section 7, 38-end.md section 11): the portal overlay intensity (+0.0125 a tick inside
*> a nether portal, -0.05 outside, PORTAL_TRIGGER at 0.25 volume and pitch random x 0.4 + 0.8 on the tick it starts), the cells of the player's box, the lerp at the partial tick,
*> the atmospheric fog of the Nether (the biome's visual/fog_color, 10 to 96) and the End (#181318, end sky box), and the End flash (window parameters from the Java LCG, the table
*> sine, no flash in window 0, the sound on the tick it starts). Expected values of the flash windows were computed with a reference script.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-DIMFX.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CLTINT.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INSIDE              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RANDOM              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEVEL               FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-PARTIAL             FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-E1                  PIC -(3)9.9999.
 01 WS-E2                  PIC -(3)9.9999.
 01 WS-E3                  PIC -(3)9.9999.
 01 WS-E4                  PIC -(3)9.9999.
 01 WS-N                   PIC -(5)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     CALL "STATE-TABLES-ENSURE" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE

*>   The portal process.
     MOVE 0 TO DX-PORTAL DX-PORTAL-OLD
     MOVE 0.5 TO WS-RANDOM
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INSIDE
     CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE WS-RANDOM
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-SOUND-VOLUME
     COMPUTE WS-E3 ROUNDED = DX-SOUND-PITCH
     MOVE DX-SOUND TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx the first tick inside a portal: intensity 0.0125, PORTAL_TRIGGER once at volume 0.25 and pitch 1.0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 " " WS-E2 " " WS-E3 " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0125    0.2500    1.0000 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE WS-RANDOM
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL-OLD
     MOVE DX-SOUND TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx the second tick: 0.0250 after 0.0125, no new sound" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 " " WS-E2 " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0250    0.0125 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0.5 TO WS-PARTIAL
     CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-LEVEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-PARTIAL WS-LEVEL
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = WS-LEVEL
     MOVE "dimfx the lerp at the partial tick 0.5 is halfway (0.01875)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0187" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE WS-RANDOM
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL
     MOVE "dimfx inside for 102 ticks the intensity is clamped at 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   1.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-INSIDE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 10
         CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE WS-RANDOM
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL
     MOVE "dimfx outside for 10 ticks it falls by 0.05 a tick to 0.5" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.5000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 20
         CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE WS-RANDOM
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-PORTAL
     MOVE "dimfx outside long enough the intensity stops at 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The cells of the player's box: state 3 is a nether_portal block (block 7).
     MOVE 7 TO ST-BLOCK(4)
     MOVE "nether_portal" TO ST-BLOCK-NAME(8)
     MOVE 3 TO WS-STATE
     MOVE 5 TO WS-X MOVE 20 TO WS-Y MOVE 5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "TEST-SET-BLOCK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE 5.5 TO PL-X
     MOVE 20.0 TO PL-Y
     MOVE 5.5 TO PL-Z
     CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-INSIDE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE
     MOVE WS-INSIDE TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx standing in the portal cell the player is inside a portal" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 8.5 TO PL-X
     CALL "DIMFX-PORTAL-INSIDE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-INSIDE
     MOVE WS-INSIDE TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx three blocks away she is not" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Fog and sky of the dimensions. The biome under the eye is the plains row (id 0): fog_color #330808 (opaque ARGB).
     MOVE 0 TO TT-PLAINS
     MOVE 4281534472 TO TB-FOGC(1)
     MOVE "minecraft:the_nether" TO PL-DIM-NAME
     CALL "DIMFX-ENV" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-R
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-G
     COMPUTE WS-E3 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-B
     MOVE "dimfx the Nether: fog colour #330808 of the biome, fog 10 to 96, skybox none, ambient #302821" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE DX-FOG-START TO WS-N
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 WS-E2 WS-E3 " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE DX-FOG-END TO WS-N
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE DX-SKYBOX TO WS-N
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE DX-FOG-SET TO WS-N
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0.2000   0.0314   0.0314 10 96 1 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-AMBIENT-R
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-AMBIENT-G
     COMPUTE WS-E3 ROUNDED = DX-AMBIENT-B
     MOVE "dimfx the Nether's ambient light is #302821 (0.1882 0.1569 0.1294)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 WS-E2 WS-E3 DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.1882   0.1569   0.1294" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO TB-FOGC(1)
     CALL "DIMFX-ENV" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-R
     MOVE "dimfx a Nether biome without fog_color has the default #000000" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "minecraft:the_end" TO PL-DIM-NAME
     CALL "DIMFX-ENV" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-R
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-G
     COMPUTE WS-E3 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-B
     MOVE DX-FOG-START TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx the End: fog colour #181318, no distances of its own, the end sky box, ambient #3f473f" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 WS-E2 WS-E3 " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE DX-FOG-END TO WS-N
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE DX-SKYBOX TO WS-N
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     COMPUTE WS-E4 ROUNDED = DX-AMBIENT-G
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0.0941   0.0745   0.0941 -1 -1 2 0.2784" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "minecraft:overworld" TO PL-DIM-NAME
     CALL "DIMFX-ENV" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "dimfx the overworld sets no fog of its own and has the overworld sky (skybox 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE DX-SKYBOX TO WS-N
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     COMPUTE WS-E4 ROUNDED = DX-FOG-SET
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0.0000 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The End flash. Window 2 (clock 1200 to 1799): offset 138, duration 296, angles -59.7091 and -1.1439.
     MOVE "minecraft:the_end" TO PL-DIM-NAME
     MOVE 300 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE DX-FLASH-WINDOW TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx clock 300 (window 0): no flash, the parameters are not computed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-E1 " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0000 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1337 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE DX-FLASH-OFFSET TO WS-N
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE "dimfx clock 1337 (window 2, phase 137, one before the offset): offset 138, no flash yet" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) " " WS-E1 DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "138    0.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE DX-FLASH-DURATION TO WS-N
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH-XA
     COMPUTE WS-E2 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH-YA
     MOVE "dimfx window 2: duration 296, x angle -59.7091, y angle -1.1439" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) " " WS-E1 " " WS-E2 DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "296  -59.7091   -1.1439" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1339 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE DX-FLASH-SOUND TO WS-N
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE "dimfx one tick after the offset the flash starts: a small intensity and the sound flag" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) " " WS-E1 DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1    0.0105" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1340 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE DX-FLASH-SOUND TO WS-N
     MOVE "dimfx the next tick the sound flag is down and the previous intensity is kept" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH-OLD
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) " " WS-E1 DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0    0.0105" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1486 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE "dimfx at offset + duration / 2 (clock 1486) the intensity peaks at 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   1.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1636 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE "dimfx after offset + duration (clock 1636: phase 436) there is no flash" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 3000 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE DX-FLASH-OFFSET TO WS-N
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH-DURATION
     MOVE "dimfx window 5 (clock 3000): offset 76 and duration 198, recomputed when the window changes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-N) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "76 198.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "minecraft:overworld" TO PL-DIM-NAME
     MOVE 1486 TO DX-CLOCK
     CALL "DIMFX-FLASH-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-E1 ROUNDED = DX-FLASH
     MOVE "dimfx a dimension without end flashes never flashes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-E1 TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "   0.0000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-DIMFX.
 COPY CLTEST.
